To get the window width and height and automatically update when the dimensions change, use the preferred `useWindowDimensions` hook [6][7]. It "automatically updates all of its values when screen size or font scale changes" [6].

```tsx
import {useWindowDimensions} from 'react-native';

const App = () => {
  const {height, width} = useWindowDimensions();

  return (
    // Your component code
  );
};
```

rn-08.answer:
To define styles with `StyleSheet.create`, pass a JavaScript object containing style definitions to the method [4]. Using `StyleSheet.create` provides static type checking against native style properties [4].

Here is an example:

```javascript
import {StyleSheet, Text, View} from 'react-native';

const LotsOfStyles = () => {
  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <Text style={styles.red}>just red</Text>
    </View>
  );
};

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    marginTop: 50,
  },
  red: {
    color: 'red',
  },
});

export default LotsOfStyles;
```

rn-09.answer:
To determine whether a screen reader is currently active, you can use the `AccessibilityInfo` API [1]. 

You can check its state asynchronously using `AccessibilityInfo.isScreenReaderEnabled()` [5][6], or listen to changes dynamically using `AccessibilityInfo.addEventListener('screenReaderChanged',...)` [5][8].

Here is an example showing both methods:

```tsx
import {useState, useEffect} from 'react';
import {AccessibilityInfo, Text, StyleSheet} from 'react-native';

const App = () => {
  const [screenReaderEnabled, setScreenReaderEnabled] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    const screenReaderChangedSubscription = AccessibilityInfo.addEventListener(
      'screenReaderChanged',
      isScreenReaderEnabled => {
        setScreenReaderEnabled(isScreenReaderEnabled);
      },
    );

    AccessibilityInfo.isScreenReaderEnabled().then(isScreenReaderEnabled => {
      setScreenReaderEnabled(isScreenReaderEnabled);
    });

    return () => {
      screenReaderChangedSubscription.remove();
    };
  }, []);

  return (
    <Text>
      The screen reader is {screenReaderEnabled? 'enabled': 'disabled'}.
    </Text>
  );
};

export default App;
```
